{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q5379483","formula":"C₂₃H₂₈O₆","hill":"C23H28O6","elements":["H","C","O"],"composition":{"C":23.0,"H":28.0,"O":6.0},"names":{"en":"Enprostil"},"descriptions":{"en":"Enprostil is a synthetic prostaglandin designed to resemble dinoprostone. Enprostil was found to be a highly potent inhibitor of gastric HCl secretion. It is an analog of prostaglandin E2 but unlike this prostaglandin, which binds to and activates all four cellular receptors viz., EP1, EP2, EP3, and EP4 receptors, enprostil is a more selective receptor agonist in that it binds to and activates primarily the EP3 receptor."},"fame":8,"pubchemCid":9978336,"mass":400.5,"charge":0,"smiles":"COC(=O)CCC=C=CC[C@H]1[C@@H]([C@H](CC1=O)O)/C=C/[C@@H](COC2=CC=CC=C2)O","inchikey":"PTOJVMZPWPAXER-FPXSIRDUSA-N","iupac":"methyl 7-[(1S,2S,3S)-3-hydroxy-2-[(E,3S)-3-hydroxy-4-phenoxybut-1-enyl]-5-oxocyclopentyl]hepta-4,5-dienoate","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"9978336","atoms":57,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":5.087,"y":-1.286,"z":-1.22,"el":"O"},{"x":4.507,"y":2.378,"z":1.643,"el":"O"},{"x":0.936,"y":-4.303,"z":-1.482,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.202,"y":-2.207,"z":0.606,"el":"O"},{"x":-2.619,"y":2.348,"z":0.376,"el":"O"},{"x":-2.796,"y":4.197,"z":-0.996,"el":"O"},{"x":3.182,"y":-0.502,"z":0.08,"el":"C"},{"x":3.022,"y":0.502,"z":1.233,"el":"C"},{"x":4.689,"y":-0.79,"z":0.049,"el":"C"},{"x":5.345,"y":0.567,"z":0.294,"el":"C"},{"x":4.311,"y":1.288,"z":1.119,"el":"C"},{"x":1.79,"y":1.38,"z":1.099,"el":"C"},{"x":2.366,"y":-1.741,"z":0.268,"el":"C"},{"x":1.443,"y":-2.167,"z":-0.607,"el":"C"},{"x":1.787,"y":2.129,"z":-0.199,"el":"C"},{"x":0.623,"y":-3.412,"z":-0.415,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.873,"y":-3.11,"z":-0.44,"el":"C"},{"x":0.845,"y":2.053,"z":-1.093,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.086,"y":1.992,"z":-2.001,